{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01134",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.13,
      "end_seconds": 6.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "afternoon, doctor they're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.14,
      "end_seconds": 11.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "thanks, that's helpful hello, please sit what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.84,
      "end_seconds": 21.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "um, so... yellow phlegm. That's why I came. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.72,
      "end_seconds": 23.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.3,
      "end_seconds": 29.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "I'm on hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 30.34,
      "end_seconds": 35.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 6.25 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.11,
      "end_seconds": 39.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.39,
      "end_seconds": 53.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.26,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I, I take Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest. Though honestly, some days I forget to take it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.29,
      "end_seconds": 62.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "oh, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called it's a small white one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.78,
      "end_seconds": 67.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.5,
      "end_seconds": 80.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.67,
      "text": "actually, um, for my mood, I believe my husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.19,
      "end_seconds": 83.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.02,
      "end_seconds": 88.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I've had it for five days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.33,
      "end_seconds": 93.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.91,
      "end_seconds": 96.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "I'd call it severe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.65,
      "end_seconds": 103.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 103.18,
      "end_seconds": 110.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.82,
      "end_seconds": 113.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "later, thanks please go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.29,
      "end_seconds": 119.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "I've been feeling feverish too, for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.88,
      "end_seconds": 123.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "how much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.69,
      "end_seconds": 126.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'd call it it severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.12,
      "end_seconds": 129.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "What eases it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.32,
      "end_seconds": 133.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Only paracetamol, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.18,
      "end_seconds": 140.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Have you had yellow phlegm before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.26,
      "end_seconds": 146.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "a bit, last year it settled by itself back then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.86,
      "end_seconds": 158.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "any ankle swelling or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.26,
      "end_seconds": 169.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "No, no ankle swelling, no weight loss. I did have wheezing at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.35,
      "end_seconds": 172.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Yes. Right, has there been any leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.5,
      "end_seconds": 175.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "No. No leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.78,
      "end_seconds": 181.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "and and what about coughing up blood or night sweats?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.47,
      "end_seconds": 186.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.77,
      "end_seconds": 194.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.56,
      "end_seconds": 198.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Um, no, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.24,
      "end_seconds": 205.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.06,
      "end_seconds": 207.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.03,
      "end_seconds": 211.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.31,
      "end_seconds": 216.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "yes, I had a varicose vein procedure, last year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.62,
      "end_seconds": 221.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "So, are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.86,
      "end_seconds": 224.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "My sister had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.52,
      "end_seconds": 231.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "Okay, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.39,
      "end_seconds": 245.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.02,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I've never smoked in my life. I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.25,
      "end_seconds": 261.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.91,
      "end_seconds": 279.18,
      "duration_seconds": 16.27,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I've had COPD, yes. Right, uh, I've had depression, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.7,
      "end_seconds": 292.5,
      "duration_seconds": 12.8,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure and depression are known to us, good to have that clear. Alright, any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.38,
      "end_seconds": 303.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 305.84,
      "end_seconds": 315.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Blood pressure 125 over 82, oxygen saturation is 93 percent, heart rate 94, respiratory rate 26."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.61,
      "end_seconds": 317.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.44,
      "end_seconds": 325.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "I'll need to to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.09,
      "end_seconds": 328.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.02,
      "end_seconds": 344.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "There are scattered wheezes on both sides and no crackles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.72,
      "end_seconds": 372.8,
      "duration_seconds": 23.08,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. So where does that leave us? This is probably an infective exacerbation of chronic lung disease. I can't rule out a pneumonia yet. I'll request a sputum sample, it'll help with purulent sputum. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 375.8,
      "end_seconds": 379.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "We have a slot Friday at 9 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.14,
      "end_seconds": 383.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Okay, I'll be there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.9,
      "end_seconds": 409.21,
      "duration_seconds": 25.31,
      "text": "let's book a chest X-ray to look into productive cough the treatment will be prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days that should help with flare of lung disease the treatment will be doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day, for five days that should help with chest infection keep using your inhaler as before and drink plenty of fluids"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.23,
      "end_seconds": 434.02,
      "duration_seconds": 19.79,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.25,
      "end_seconds": 436.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "yes, will do"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.88,
      "end_seconds": 451.85,
      "duration_seconds": 12.97,
      "text": "Please don't wait if you become more breathless or your lips turn blue. That's when to be seen urgently. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.5,
      "end_seconds": 456.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}